      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A study of isotope scanning in children with irritable hip syndrome has demonstrated its role as a discriminator between Perthes disease and transient synovitis. Three children with normal radiographs had Perthes changes on scanning and went on to develop X-ray changes. An anatomical and pathological basis for the scan abnormalities is suggested."},
